            <ArticleTitle>[Improved regional myocardial function after aortocoronary bypass surgery noninvasive studies using the first-pass technic].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>583-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>50 patients after coronary artery bypass grafting were matched with 50 not-operated patients. After a follow-up period of four years they were investigated by first pass radionuclide angiography. Revascularized myocardial areas showed significantly higher regional ejection fraction during exercise and in territories with prior myocardial infarction. The results proved the hemodynamic benefits of coronary artery bypass grafting even in territories with poor myocardial function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
